{"name":"Wax Poetic","hex":"#f1e6cc","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wax poetic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become increasingly verbose.","To speak in an increasingly verbose manner, as if constructing poetry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wax_poetic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wax Poetic","blocks":[{"text":"Wax Poetic is a New York-based trip hop band. The band came together in 1997 founded by Turkish musician Ilhan Erşahin, who is still a current member, playing tenor saxophone and keys. The group originated at the now defunct club Save the Robots, and consisted of a group of musicians jamming together. The band's music is noted for its \"heavy groove of drum and bass, blended with quick dance elements.\" The band signed to Atlantic Records in the late '90s and released their debut self-titled album in June 2000."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wax_Poetic","wikidata":"Q3077714"},{"title":"Wax","blocks":[{"text":"Waxes are a diverse class of organic compounds that are lipophilic solids that are malleable near ambient temperatures. They include higher alkanes and lipids, typically with melting points above about 40 °C (104 °F), melting to give low viscosity liquids. Waxes are insoluble in water but soluble in nonpolar organic solvents such as hexane, benzene and chloroform. Natural waxes of various types are produced by plants and animals and occur in petroleum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Beeswax_foundation.jpg/330px-Beeswax_foundation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wax","wikidata":"Q124695"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Beeswax_foundation.jpg/500px-Beeswax_foundation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Beeswax_foundation.j